{'symbol': 'SYF', 'date': '2023-04-26 09:00:00', 'title': 'SYNCHRONY STUDY ESTIMATES THE LIFETIME COST OF HORSE OWNERSHIP RANGES FROM $300,000 TO $924,000', 'text': 'HORSE OWNERS UNDERESTIMATE THE TOTAL COST OF CARE,\xa0 WITH ACTUAL EXPENSES THREE OR EVEN FOUR-PLUS TIMES HIGHER\xa0\xa0 RESEARCH UNCOVERS 85 PERCENT OF HORSE OWNERS FEEL ANXIETY FROM HORSE EXPENSES,\xa0CAN EXPECT ONE TO TWO COSTLY EMERGENCY MEDICAL EVENTS PER YEAR\xa0 STAMFORD, CONN. , APRIL 26, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- HORSE OWNERS NATIONWIDE VASTLY UNDERESTIMATE THE LIFETIME COST OF CARING FOR A HORSE, WHICH RANGES FROM NEARLY $300,000 TO $924,000, ACCORDING TO A NEW SYNCHRONY (NYSE: SYF) STUDY, "EQUINE LIFETIME OF CARE.'}